{"ref":"BDB, זָקָן","hw":"זָקָן","html":"† <big><span dir=\"rtl\">זָקָן</span></big>  <strong>n.m.</strong> <sup><a data-ref=\"II Samuel 10:5\" href=\"/II_Samuel.10.5\">2 S 10:5</a></sup> + <strong>beard and f.</strong> <sup><a data-ref=\"Isaiah 15:2\" href=\"/Isaiah.15.2\">Is 15:2</a></sup> + <strong>chin (</strong>Assyrian <em>ziḳnu</em>, Asrb. <sup>Annals iv. 29</sup>; Arabic <span dir=\"rtl\">ذَقَنٌ</span>, Aramaic <span dir=\"rtl\">דְּקַן</span>, <span dir=\"rtl\">ܕܩܰܢ</span> <strong>)</strong>—abs. <span dir=\"rtl\">ז׳</span> <a data-ref=\"Leviticus 13:20\" href=\"/Leviticus.13.20\">Lv 13:20</a> +; cstr. <span dir=\"rtl\">זְקַן</span> <a data-ref=\"II Samuel 20:9\" href=\"/II_Samuel.20.9\">2 S 20:9</a> +; sf. <span dir=\"rtl\">זְקָנִי</span> <a data-ref=\"Ezra 9:3\" href=\"/Ezra.9.3\">Ezr 9:3</a>; <span dir=\"rtl\">זְקָנֶ֑ךָ</span> <a data-ref=\"Leviticus 19:27\" href=\"/Leviticus.19.27\">Lv 19:27</a> <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 5:1\" href=\"/Ezekiel.5.1\">Ez 5:1</a>; <span dir=\"rtl\">זְקָנוֹ</span> <a data-ref=\"I Samuel 21:14\" href=\"/I_Samuel.21.14\">1 S 21:14</a> + 2 times; <span dir=\"rtl\">זְקַנְכֶם</span> <a data-ref=\"II Samuel 10:5\" href=\"/II_Samuel.10.5\">2 S 10:5</a> <a data-ref=\"I Chronicles 19:5\" href=\"/I_Chronicles.19.5\">1 Ch 19:5</a>; <span dir=\"rtl\">זְקָנָם</span> <a data-ref=\"II Samuel 10:4\" href=\"/II_Samuel.10.4\">2 S 10:4</a> <a data-ref=\"Leviticus 21:5\" href=\"/Leviticus.21.5\">Lv 21:5</a>; never pl.—<br><strong>1.</strong>  <em>chin</em> (opp. <span dir=\"rtl\">רֹאשׁ</span>, top of head) <a data-ref=\"Leviticus 13:29\" href=\"/Leviticus.13.29\">Lv 13:29</a>, <a data-ref=\"Leviticus 13:30\" href=\"/Leviticus.13.30\">30</a>; <a data-ref=\"Leviticus 14:9\" href=\"/Leviticus.14.9\">14:9</a> (all P), <a data-ref=\"II Samuel 20:9\" href=\"/II_Samuel.20.9\">2 S 20:9</a> <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 5:1\" href=\"/Ezekiel.5.1\">Ez 5:1</a>; cf. also <a data-ref=\"I Samuel 21:14\" href=\"/I_Samuel.21.14\">1 S 21:14</a> <a data-ref=\"Psalms 133:2\" href=\"/Psalms.133.2\">ψ 133:2</a> (where however chin as <em>bearded</em> may be meant); chin, or lower jaw, of lion and bear <a data-ref=\"I Samuel 17:35\" href=\"/I_Samuel.17.35\">1 S 17:35</a>.<br><strong>2.</strong>  <em>beard</em>, as growing <span dir=\"rtl\">(צמח)</span> <a data-ref=\"II Samuel 10:5\" href=\"/II_Samuel.10.5\">2 S 10:5</a> = <a data-ref=\"I Chronicles 19:5\" href=\"/I_Chronicles.19.5\">1 Ch 19:5</a>; as cut off <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 7:20\" href=\"/Isaiah.7.20\">Is 7:20</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">(ספה)</span>, <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 15:2\" href=\"/Isaiah.15.2\">15:2</a> = <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 48:37\" href=\"/Jeremiah.48.37\">Je 48:37</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">(גרע)</span>; cf. <span dir=\"rtl\">מְגֻלְּחֵי זָקָן</span> <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 41:5\" href=\"/Jeremiah.41.5\">Je 41:5</a> <a data-ref=\"II Samuel 10:4\" href=\"/II_Samuel.10.4\">2 S 10:4</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">(גלח)</span>; <span dir=\"rtl\">שׂער ראשׁי וּזְקָנִי</span> <a data-ref=\"Ezra 9:3\" href=\"/Ezra.9.3\">Ezr 9:3</a>; here belongs <span dir=\"rtl\">פאת זקן(ך)</span> <a data-ref=\"Leviticus 19:27\" href=\"/Leviticus.19.27\">Lv 19:27</a>; <a data-ref=\"Leviticus 21:5\" href=\"/Leviticus.21.5\">21:5</a> (both H; opp. <span dir=\"rtl\">ראשׁ</span>).","next":"BDB, זָקֵן","prev":"BDB, זקן"}